  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nTo contest a BIR assessment, you do not need to file a return and a protest at the same time. Instead, you must file a protest against the assessment within 30 days from the date of receipt of the Formal Letter of Demand (FLD) or Final Assessment Notice (FAN) (Section 228, NIRC). \n\nThe protest can be a request for reconsideration or reinvestigation, depending on whether you are challenging the assessment based on existing records or presenting new evidence (RR 18-2013). If you fail to file a valid protest within the prescribed period, the assessment will become final, executory, and demandable (RR 18-2013). \n\nIn summary, while you must file a protest within the specified timeframe, there is no requirement to file a return simultaneously.\n\n### Relevant Facts / Assumptions\nThe factual circumstances have not been fully described. The analysis is based on the question as presented.\n\n### Alternative Interpretations\nNo alternative interpretations identified from the available indexed authorities.\n\n### Position Strength\nPosition strength is preliminary and subject to full fact pattern verification.",
